  },
  "rule": "Each connected blue (1) structure of rectangular blocks joined by 1-wide corridors contains one seed cell of another colour inside a block interior; paint the interior (block minus its 1-cell border) of every block in that structure with the seed colour. Corridors and block borders stay blue.",
  "scope": "Supported: random grid sizes 14..30 per side; 2-4 structures per grid; each structure is a tree of 2-9 blocks (up to four on smaller canvases) (3x3 up to 8x12) linked by straight 1-wide corridors of length 1-6 attached at non-corner border cells; the seed is placed in a random block interior; seed colours are distinct per grid and drawn from 2..9; blocks may touch the grid edge. Fixed: background 0 and shape colour 1. Not supported: cycles between blocks, corridors bending or joining corridor-to-corridor, multiple seeds per structure, blocks touching each other directly, structures with no seed, or scenes where filled cells exceed 48% of the grid.",
  "constraints": [
    "Every block is at least 3x3, so it has a nonempty interior.",
    "Corridors are exactly 1 cell wide and attach to a non-corner border cell of the parent block.",
    "New cells must not touch any existing cell in the 8-neighbourhood, except the first corridor cell touching its parent block. Different structures therefore never touch, even diagonally.",
    "As a result, the cells whose 8 neighbours are all filled are exactly the latent block interiors.",
    "Each structure has exactly one seed, and it lies strictly inside a block interior.",
    "Seed colours are distinct within a grid and never 0 or 1.",
    "Filled cells cover at most 48% of the grid, so background 0 is clearly the most common colour and blue 1 is the most common non-background colour. This fixes the earlier failures, where blue outnumbered the background.",
    "The output always differs from the input, because every block has a nonempty interior and at least one interior cell besides the seed or another block exists in each structure of 2+ blocks."
  ],
  "known_limitations": [
    "Structures are trees grown from a start block, so the loops that occasionally appear in real ARC layouts are not generated.",
    "Corridors are always straight and run block-to-block.",
    "Bounded rejection sampling enforces a 48% fill cap to preserve the saved solver's majority-background assumption. Failure raises explicitly; no scene/count fallback is used.",
    "Validation fixtures are reproduced from hand-extracted latent block and corridor lists passed explicitly to generate(); the random path never samples them."
  ],
